{"id": "sllama0004", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The space telescope launched in 1990 is called the Hubble Space Teles cope. It's named after Edwin Hubble, a famous astronomer. This telescope has revolutionized our understanding of the universe by capturing detailed images of distant galaxies and stars from orbit above Earth' s atmosphere.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0012", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The peregrine falcon is the fastest flying bird. It can reach speeds of over 2 40 miles per hour when diving, making it the fastest bird in level flight as well.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0020", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Olympic sport that involves throwing a javelin is called javelin throw. It's part of the track and field events in the Olympics. A javelin is a long, pointed stick that athletes throw as far as they can, aiming to get the best distance possible. It requires strength, skill, and technique to throw it effectively.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0028", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": null, "no_speak": true, "answer_text": "", "eot_seen": false, "n_ans_chunks": 0, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0036", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The person with the most Olympic gold medals in any sport is swimmer Michael Phelps from the United States. He won 2 3 gold medal s during his career at the Summer Olympic Game s. That's more than anyone else has ever won.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0044", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Ten divided by two is five. It' s a pretty straightforward division problem, and the answer is simply five.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0052", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The theory of evolution was discovered by Charles Darwin.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0060", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The highest mountain peak in the contiguous United States is Mount Wh itney, located in California. It reach es an elevation of about 14,5 05 feet, or roughly 4,4 2 5 meters above sea level.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0068", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest city in the Midwest is Chicago, Illinois. It's not only the biggest by population but also one of the most important cultural and economic centers in the region.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0076", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "David Beckham's sport is soccer. He' s a professional football er who played for teams like Manchester United and Real Mad rid, as well as the England national team.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0084", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The animal known for its distinctive black and white stripes is the z ebrafish. These fish have bold horizontal stripe s that make them easily recognizable.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0092", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for so dium is Na.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0100", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The highest attended tennis tournament is the US Open. It' s held in New York City and attract s huge crowds, especially during peak matches or when top players compete. While exact numbers vary from year to year, it often sees more attendees than other major tournaments like Wimbledon or the French Open.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0108", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The fruit known as the apple of South east Asia is the mango. It' s highly valued in region for its sweet flavor and juicy texture, making it a popular treat across many countries like India, Thailand, and the Philip pines.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0116", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A lobster has 1 0 claw-like append ages called ch ellicera e.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0124", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for boron is B. It's a light metal that' s commonly found in minerals like borax and is used in various industrial applications.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0132", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The only golfer to win all four major tournament s in the same year is Jack Nickla us. He achieved this incredible feat in 19 8 6, winning the Masters, U S Open, The Open Championship, and the PGA Championship.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0140", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest mall in the United States is located in the city of Miami. It' s called the Mall of America, and it covers an area of over 5 00,000 square feet.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0148", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Tom Brady has won the most Super Bowl rings as a player, with seven championship s under his belt.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0156", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The highest-gro ssing film of all time, world wide, is Ta king of Ga laxia. It's a Chinese historical epic, and it earned over 5 billion US dollars globally.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0164", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In Sikhism, there is one central gu ru known as the Guru Granth Sahib. This sacred text is considered the ultimate spiritual guide and is revered by Sikhs worldwide. So, while there were ten historical human gurus in the past, today the Guru Granth Sa hib stands as the eternal guru for all Sikhs.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0172", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The spacecraft that landed on Mars in 2012 was called Curiosity. It's a rover sent by NASA to explore the surface of Mars and look for signs of past life.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0180", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The largest canyon in the world is the Grand Can yon, located in Arizona, USA. It stretches over 4 4 6 miles long, up to 18 miles wide, and reaches depths of more than a mile. While not the deepest or widest canyon globally, its sheer scale, dramatic layer ed rock formations, and iconic status make it the most famous and often considered the largest in terms of overall size.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0188", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It's actually quite complicated, because Hindu ism doesn't have a single supreme god. Instead, there are many gods and goddesses who are worshipped depending on the region or tradition. However, some people consider Bra hman to be the ultimate reality or supreme being that underlies all existence. Other common deities include B rama, Vishnu, and Shiva, often referred to as the Trim urty. So while there isn't one absolute answer, the concept of Brah man represents the highest form of divinity in Hindu philosophy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0196", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for sulfur is S. It comes from the Latin word for sulfur, which is sulfurum. So, just remember S for su lfur!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0204", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Michael Ke aton played the role of Ba tman in the 1989 movie.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0212", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Canada is border ed by the United States, and Mexico is also bordered by the United States. So the country that borders both Canada and Mexico is the United States of America.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0220", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chemical symbol for platinum is P t.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 3, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0228", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The actor who played Luke Sky walker in the original Star Wars trilogy was Mark Hamill. He appeared as the character in all three films from A New Hope to The E mperor's New Groove, and his performance helped define the role of Luke Skywalker for generations of fans.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 15, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0236", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Seven times three is twenty-one.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 2, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "sllama0244", "pool": "sllama", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The chamele on is known for its unique ability to change its body color. They can shift from green to brown or even blue, depending on their mood, temperature, and surroundings. This color change helps them blend into their environment for protection or communication with other chameleons. It ’s a really fascinating adaptation!", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
